EENNVVIIRROONNMMEENNTT
       DEBIAN_HAS_FRONTEND
              If  this  environment variable is set and the ----ddrryy--rruunn flag was
              not given, uuppddaattee--ppaasssswwdd uses debconf to prompt for  whether  to
              make  changes.   Each  proposed  change  will produce a separate
              prompt.  User or group removals, UID or GID  changes,  and  home
              directory  changes  will  be  asked with high priority.  User or
              group additions and shell changes will be asked with medium pri‐
              ority.   Questions  about  whether to move entries above the NIS
              compat inclusion entry or whether to change the GECOS of a  user
              are asked at low priority.

BBUUGGSS
       At  this  moment  uuppddaattee--ppaasssswwdd  does  not  verify the shadow-file.  It
       should check if the entries in the passwd are also in shadow  and  vice
       versa, and that passwords are not present in both files.

